// Generated from Noir Math Library Specification
// Fixed-point arithmetic library for DeFi operations

Math::add
├── When y is positive
│   ├── When x + y does not overflow
│   │   └── It should return x + y
│   └── When x + y would overflow U128_MAX
│       └── It should revert with "overflow"
├── When y is negative
│   ├── When x >= |y|
│   │   └── It should return x - |y|
│   └── When x < |y|
│       └── It should revert with "underflow"
└── When y is zero
    └── It should return x unchanged

Math::sub
├── When y is positive
│   ├── When x >= y
│   │   └── It should return x - y
│   └── When x < y
│       └── It should revert with "underflow"
├── When y is negative
│   ├── When x + |y| does not overflow
│   │   └── It should return x + |y|
│   └── When x + |y| would overflow U128_MAX
│       └── It should revert with "overflow"
└── When y is zero
    └── It should return x unchanged

Math::mul
├── When y is zero
│   └── It should return 0
├── When x exceeds I64_MAX
│   └── It should revert with "x > max int128"
├── When y equals I64_MIN
│   ├── When x is zero
│   │   └── It should return 0
│   ├── When x * (I64_MAX + 1) does not overflow
│   │   └── It should return -(x * (I64_MAX + 1))
│   └── When x * (I64_MAX + 1) would overflow
│       └── It should revert with "mul overflow"
├── When y is positive
│   ├── When x * y does not overflow I64_MAX
│   │   └── It should return x * y as i64
│   └── When x * y would overflow I64_MAX
│       └── It should revert with "mul overflow"
└── When y is negative
    ├── When x * |y| does not overflow I64_MAX + 1
    │   └── It should return -(x * |y|) as i64
    └── When x * |y| would overflow I64_MAX + 1
        └── It should revert with "mul overflow"

Math::min
├── When x equals y
│   └── It should return x
├── When x is less than y
│   └── It should return x
└── When x is greater than y
    └── It should return y

Math::max
├── When x equals y
│   └── It should return x
├── When x is greater than y
│   └── It should return x
└── When x is less than y
    └── It should return y

Math::diff
├── When x equals y
│   └── It should return 0
├── When x is greater than y
│   ├── When difference fits in I64_MAX
│   │   └── It should return (x - y) as i64
│   └── When difference exceeds I64_MAX
│       └── It should revert with "diff overflow"
└── When x is less than y
    ├── When difference magnitude fits in I64_MIN
    │   └── It should return -(y - x) as i64
    └── When difference magnitude exceeds I64_MIN
        └── It should revert with "diff overflow"

Math::to_rad
├── When wad is zero
│   └── It should return 0 as Field
├── When wad * 10^27 does not overflow Field
│   └── It should return wad * 10^27 as Field
└── When wad * 10^27 would overflow Field
    └── It should revert with "to_rad overflow"

Math::wmul
├── When either x or y is zero
│   └── It should return 0
├── When x * y / WAD does not overflow
│   ├── When result rounds down
│   │   └── It should return (x * y) / WAD
│   └── When result is exact
│       └── It should return (x * y) / WAD
└── When x * y would overflow U128_MAX
    └── It should revert with "wmul overflow"

Math::wdiv
├── When y is zero
│   └── It should revert with "division by zero"
├── When x is zero
│   └── It should return 0
├── When x * WAD / y does not overflow
│   ├── When result rounds down
│   │   └── It should return (x * WAD) / y
│   └── When result is exact
│       └── It should return (x * WAD) / y
└── When x * WAD would overflow U128_MAX
    └── It should revert with "wdiv overflow"

Math::rmul
├── When either x or y is zero
│   └── It should return 0
├── When x * y / RAY does not overflow
│   ├── When result rounds down
│   │   └── It should return (x * y) / RAY
│   └── When result is exact
│       └── It should return (x * y) / RAY
└── When x * y would overflow U128_MAX
    └── It should revert with "rmul overflow"

Math::rdiv
├── When y is zero
│   └── It should revert with "division by zero"
├── When x is zero
│   └── It should return 0
├── When x * RAY / y does not overflow
│   ├── When result rounds down
│   │   └── It should return (x * RAY) / y
│   └── When result is exact
│       └── It should return (x * RAY) / y
└── When x * RAY would overflow U128_MAX
    └── It should revert with "rdiv overflow"

Math::rpow
├── When n is 0
│   └── It should return base (representing 1)
├── When n is 1
│   └── It should return x
├── When x is 0
│   └── It should return 0
├── When x is base (representing 1)
│   └── It should return base
└── When computing x^n
    ├── When using binary exponentiation
    │   ├── When intermediate results do not overflow
    │   │   └── It should return x^n with base precision
    │   └── When intermediate results would overflow
    │       └── It should revert with "rpow overflow"
    └── When result needs rounding
        └── It should round down to nearest integer

MathInvariants
├── It should maintain overflow protection across all operations
├── It should preserve precision in WAD/RAY/RAD conversions
├── It should enforce commutative property for min and max
├── It should prevent division by zero in wdiv and rdiv
└── It should handle I64_MIN edge case correctly in mul